# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Demo deployment
#
# This file makes a hosted build run PL·CE against its in-memory
# marketplace instead of a database. It is committed on purpose so a
# deploy works with no dashboard configuration — the flag is a mode
# switch, not a secret.
#
# WHAT THIS MEANS IN PRODUCTION
#
#   The database lives in the server's memory. It is seeded on first
#   request and lost on every cold start, and on a serverless host each
#   instance keeps its own copy — so two visitors can disagree about
#   what exists, and anything anyone creates disappears without notice.
#
#   Fine for a link someone clicks to look around. Wrong for anything
#   whose data is supposed to survive.
#
# GOING LIVE
#
#   Delete this file, then set NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY on the host and run the migrations in
#   supabase/migrations. Leaving the flag behind is survivable — real
#   credentials take precedence over it — but deleting it restores the
#   guard that catches a credential typo, so delete it.
#
#   Setting only one of the two Supabase variables always fails loudly,
#   flag or no flag. See `assertNotAccidentalDemoMode` in src/lib/env.ts.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ALLOW_DEMO_MODE=true
